     l _n  to set the amount of lookahead used by the machine in
          searching for moves.  Zero means none at all. Four is
          the default.  Greater than six means you may fall
          asleep waiting for the machine to move.

     t _n  to tell _r_e_v_e_r_s_i that you will only need _n seconds to
          consider each move. If you fail to respond in the
          alloted time, you forfeit your turn.

     If _r_e_v_e_r_s_i is given a file name as an argument, it will
     checkpoint the game, move by move, by dumping the board onto
     _f_i_l_e.  The -r option will cause _r_e_v_e_r_s_i to restart the game
     from _f_i_l_e and continue logging.

